Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• `Sides.Side`: to isolate only LONG-side trades.  
• `Sides.PartyIDs.PartyID`: often embeds desk / strategy identifiers such as “feeling‑lucky” or “momentum”.  
• `StrikePrice` / `LastPx`: can be combined as `StrikePrice‑LastPx` to approximate “intrinsic value”.  
• `TradeDate` / `TransactTime`: optional date filters if we want a time window.  

Typical WHERE‑clauses you may need  
• `UNNEST(Sides) s  WHERE s.Side = 'LONG'` –– long‑side filter  
• `UNNEST(s.PartyIDs) p  WHERE LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%feeling-lucky%'` –– feeling‑lucky strategy  
• `UNNEST(s.PartyIDs) p  WHERE LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%momentum%'` –– momentum strategy  

Below are ten exploratory → analytical queries (each capped at 20 rows) that gradually narrow the data and finally produce the requested comparison.

```sql
-- 1. Peek at raw rows
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. All distinct side values that appear inside the Sides array
SELECT DISTINCT s.Side
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report`,
UNNEST(Sides) AS s
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. All distinct PartyRole values; helps discover which role contains strategy information
SELECT DISTINCT p.PartyRole
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report`,
UNNEST(Sides) s,
UNNEST(s.PartyIDs) p
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Inspect PartyID strings that include the word “lucky”
SELECT DISTINCT p.PartyID
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report`,
UNNEST(Sides) s,
UNNEST(s.PartyIDs) p
WHERE LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%lucky%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Inspect PartyID strings that include the word “momentum”
SELECT DISTINCT p.PartyID
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report`,
UNNEST(Sides) s,
UNNEST(s.PartyIDs) p
WHERE LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%momentum%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Compute an intrinsic value field for a sample of LONG trades
SELECT
  StrikePrice,
  LastPx,
  StrikePrice - LastPx AS intrinsic_value
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report`,
UNNEST(Sides) s
WHERE s.Side = 'LONG'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Average intrinsic value for LONG trades using the feeling‑lucky strategy
SELECT
  AVG(StrikePrice - LastPx) AS avg_intrinsic_value_lucky
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report`,
UNNEST(Sides) s,
UNNEST(s.PartyIDs) p
WHERE s.Side = 'LONG'
  AND LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%feeling-lucky%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Average intrinsic value for LONG trades using the momentum strategy
SELECT
  AVG(StrikePrice - LastPx) AS avg_intrinsic_value_momentum
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report`,
UNNEST(Sides) s,
UNNEST(s.PartyIDs) p
WHERE s.Side = 'LONG'
  AND LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%momentum%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Compare both averages side‑by‑side
SELECT
  AVG(CASE WHEN LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%feeling-lucky%' THEN StrikePrice - LastPx END) AS avg_intrinsic_value_lucky,
  AVG(CASE WHEN LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%momentum%'       THEN StrikePrice - LastPx END) AS avg_intrinsic_value_momentum
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report`,
UNNEST(Sides) s,
UNNEST(s.PartyIDs) p
WHERE s.Side = 'LONG'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final answer: how much higher is feeling‑lucky vs momentum (difference in points)
SELECT
  AVG(CASE WHEN LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%feeling-lucky%' THEN StrikePrice - LastPx END)
      - 
  AVG(CASE WHEN LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%momentum%' THEN StrikePrice - LastPx END)
      AS intrinsic_value_diff
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report`,
UNNEST(Sides) s,
UNNEST(s.PartyIDs) p
WHERE s.Side = 'LONG'
LIMIT 20;
```

Run query 10 to obtain the numeric difference—the amount by which the average intrinsic value of feeling‑lucky long trades exceeds that of momentum long trades.
